issues.problem:
Round 6 wrote four sentences about V1's ctrld sweep (24,221 copies, every part of every 5th plausible design with a cleaned part, from #1 and #3):
- 'the 22,243 others keep it valid' (E-S2.14);
- 'the 22,243 others keep the design valid' (M3-notes);
- 'of 22,243 such copies that leave the sword valid' (plain words, Round 5 item);
- 'the 22,243 that leave the sword valid were measured' (plain words, Round 6 item).

They are false. My ctrlvalid (work/ctrlvalid.luau, out/cv_live_1.txt and cv_live_3.txt) validated every copy as Analyze.run reports it, plus the MAX_PARTS count:
- 1,858 take a slot past its maximum (930 + 928, SlotTooMany);
- 120 only exceed MAX_PARTS (60 + 60, valid otherwise);
- 21,628 are valid (10,913 + 10,715);
- 615 (314 + 301) copy parts of 105 designs that are invalid without any copy.

The 105 designs (out/baseinvalid2.txt) are 96 tiled and 9 grille, all SlotMissing Blade/Cleaned (V5), e.g. #32801 `grille|0.6 x 1.2 x 0.02 4 x 2 f0.9` and #33006 `tiled|0.6 x 1.2 x 0.02 tiles 1 x 1 hair 1e-05`. ctrld measured those copies only because it passes measureInvalid, and the game never measures those swords.

So 615 of the 22,243 neither keep nor leave the design valid. The sweep's 'none moves' still holds for them.

Also checked so the figure stays right: f7ac37d's 38 moved copies are on 19 valid designs and stay within every limit (out/valid19.txt, count19.txt). Its '38 copies on 19 designs, up to 6.9 g' stands.

